{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
============================================================================
 app_konference (Asterisk 20) installed.

 This port provides ONLY the conferencing module (app_konference.so).
 It builds against the OFFICIAL net/asterisk20 port.

 If your dialplan uses SIP/ channels (legacy chan_sip), note that in the
 official net/asterisk20 port chan_sip is the "SIP" option and it is OFF
 by default. A typical option set:

     SIP     (legacy chan_sip, if you use SIP/ channels)
     PGSQL   (PostgreSQL realtime/CDR, optional)
     SRTP, PJSIP, CURL          (defaults, keep enabled)

 WebRTC (browser softphone) needs PJSIP (res_pjsip + transport wss),
 SRTP (DTLS-SRTP), res_http_websocket + OpenSSL (built by default).

 Example (one host):
     cd /usr/ports/net/asterisk20 && make config      # tick SIP if needed
     make install clean
     cd /usr/ports/net/asterisk20-appkonference && make install clean

 Reproducible (no dialog), set options then build:
     make -C /usr/ports/net/asterisk20 \
          OPTIONS_SET="SIP PGSQL PJSIP SRTP CURL" \
          OPTIONS_UNSET="MYSQL" config-recursive
     make -C /usr/ports/net/asterisk20 reinstall clean
     make -C /usr/ports/net/asterisk20-appkonference reinstall clean

 After install, load the module in /usr/local/etc/asterisk/modules.conf:
     load => app_konference.so
 and verify from CLI:
     asterisk -rx "module show like konference"

 Both ULAW and ALAW are compiled in.
============================================================================
EOM
